<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liberal Revolution of 1820</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1820</span> · Also known as Liberal Revolution</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Liberal Revolution of 1820 was a constitutionalist uprising in Portugal, beginning in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a>. It demanded a constitution and the return of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> VI from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, where the court had lived since 1808. The king's return and Portuguese attempts to reduce Brazil's status led to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grito-do-ipiranga">Brazilian independence</a> in 1822 and the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liberal-revolution-of-1820.jpg" alt="Liberal Revolution of 1820" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oscar Pereira da Silva · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sess%C3%A3o_das_Cortes_de_Lisboa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
